  "rationale": "Genome-wide KO screen in LNCaP prostate cancer cells (Brunello-like, 4 guides/gene, 142 non-cutting controls: LacZ 96, luciferase 24, EGFP 22). Per-sample count files (GSE226977_RAW.tar) were merged on sgRNA. 12 libraries: T0 and final time point (TF), each with DMSO and enzalutamide (EZ), 3 replicates. The paper's screen contrasts enzalutamide vs DMSO at the final time point: sensitizers (e.g. HOXA9) deplete in EZ. Primary analysis TF-EZ vs TF-DMSO with median-ratio totals, because the final EZ libraries are severely bottlenecked (17-21% of guides at zero, top 1% of guides hold 23-33% of reads), so library totals call most genes depleted. A library-totals run is kept to show the swing. No T0-anchored design: the deposited T0-DMSO and T0-EZ labels appear swapped (T0-EZ-Rep1 alone shows a bottleneck the other T0 libraries do not), and T0 is a single pre-treatment pool split by label, so anchoring to it is not reliable."
